    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d555">

                <pb facs="0541" n="465" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg465"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115C96/60</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Silliman to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Querétaro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 19, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The text has been furnished me of decree declaring that on account of connection
                    with the Santa Ysabel massacre<anchor n="2" xml:id="d555-f1"/> Francisco Villa,
                    Rafael Castro and Pablo Lopez are outside the law, and that any citizen may
                    apprehend and execute them, the only formality being their identification.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d555-f1" n="2" xml:id="d555-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">See</hi> Protection of Americans and American interests,
                        <ref target="#pg653">p. 653</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
